    "title": "Storrs bars and restaurants prepare for excited UConn fans as watch parties heat up",
    "text": "Local eateries near UConn, like Hops44 and Red Rock Cafe, are buzzing with excitement as they gear up for watch parties during this weekend's Final Four games. STORRS, Conn. — Local restaurants and bars near UConn's campus in Storrs have been preparing for large crowds and a lot of noise during this weekend's Final Four games. Nancy Mckenney, owner of Hops44 in Storrs, says the energy in the sports bar during watch parties is unmatched. “People are going to be on the edge of their seats if we win [Saturday] night and if we win [Friday] we’re going to the big games. This is incredible again for UConn,” said Mckenney. To prepare for the huge crowds, the business has extra staff ready to clock in and serve excited and loyal Huskies fans. They also have specials on food like bang-bang shrimp and their meatloaf BLT. “These people that have come all season to watch it. We want to share it with them just like they want to share it with us,” said Mckenney. Just down the road, Simon Mavridis, the general manager of the Red Rock Cafe in Storrs, says they're super excited to host. “It’s a great vibe. We all get into the game,” said Mavridis. He says moments like these hold a special place in his heart. “I'm a UConn alumni, I went to school at UConn and met my wife there. It’s like I never left home,” said Mavridis. Both restaurants will be hosting watch parties for both the men's and women’s games on a first come, first serve basis. ---- Alyshia Hercules is a Multi-Skilled Journalist for FOX61 News. She can be reached at AHercules@FOX61.com. Follow her on Facebook or X. ---- Do you have a story idea or something on your mind you want to share? We want to hear from you! Email us at newstips@fox61.com. ---- HERE ARE MORE WAYS TO GET FOX61 NEWS Download the FOX61 News APP iTunes: Click here to download Google Play: Click here to download Stream Live on ROKU: Add the channel from the ROKU store or by searching FOX61. Steam Live on FIRE TV: Search ‘FOX61’ and click ‘Ge